Where long has 32 bits, as in wasm32, the spaced seed and toggle masks,
64-bit numbers, are read with strtol, which stops at 2^31 - 1: read them
with strtoll, which is what strtol is natively.

The leading zeros of a 64-bit hash, for the distinct minimizers of a report
(-K), are counted with __builtin_clzl, which takes a long: count them with
__builtin_clzll.

